ng validated outputs.", "before": "Retained bytes are not a registration. The producer interface that owns the operation owns its output schema, so the schema is registered exactly when the Plan-selected producer closure carries it at the tree path for that operation; a new operation is registered by shipping its interface document in the admitted closure, never by a host or platform table.", "parent": {"bytes": 196987, "path": "docs/coop/design-corrections/foundation/identity-schemas.v3.json", "sha256": "a76c9e2f07e8f8e52ee611f157548f6a09061866308652e3a0f7e3c24893db21"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/$defs/stage-spec/properties/outputSchemaDigest/x-opensip-digest/registeredBy/law"}}, {"after": "Retained bytes are not a registration. The producer interface that owns the operation owns its output schema, so the schema is registered exactly when the Plan-selected producer closure carries it at the tree path for that operation; a new operation is registered by shipping its interface document in the admitted closure, never by a host or platform table. Document validation uses the stage-meta-reference-selection-v1 structural profile: the eight pinned Draft2020-12 default meta-schema resources with format annotations not asserted. Fixed meta-schema pattern assertions retain their published trailing-LF compatibility. Producer regex strings and references remain inert at registration; structurally admitted metadata does not certify regex compilation or instance execution. Any execution owner must separately declare deterministic executable-schema semantics and refuse unsupported or invalid schemas before claiming validated outputs.", "before": "Retained bytes are not a registration. The producer interface that owns the operation owns its output schema, so the schema is registered exactly when the Plan-selected producer closure carries it at the tree path for that operation; a new operation is registered by shipping its interface document in the admitted closure, never by a host or platform table.", "parent": {"bytes": 197480, "path": "docs/implementation/m1/source-selection-v2/schemas/sources/identity.v3.schema.json", "sha256": "311c1feb09ff8cd0b207233d2ec0d7440bb1c72fc0470de277ee1891c24bb68f"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/$defs/stage-spec/properties/outputSchemaDigest/x-opensip-digest/registeredBy/law"}}, {"after": "spec's own `operation` and `outputDomains`. The stage-meta-reference-selection-v1 profile validates against eight pinned Draft2020-12 default meta-schema resources with format annotations not asserted, preserving the two fixed meta-schema pattern assertions (including their trailing-LF compatibility). Registration does not compile producer regex strings or execute schema instances: invalid regex strings can be structurally registered, and an execution owner must separately select deterministic executable-schema semantics and fail closed before claiming validated outputs. This explicit successor changes the former ambient regex-format assertion; optional packages cannot change registration. Each failure refuses by its own name:", "before": "spec's own `operation` and `outputDomains`. Each failure refuses by its own name:", "parent": {"bytes": 135448, "path": "docs/v2/contracts/product-v1/identity-and-evidence.md", "sha256": "c82404f3a0cf56fa6cc02e99cc3ebbd5356fedc3b36aeb38f9ef284077fbd31f"}, "selector": {"line": 1314}}], "passageSupersessions": [], "selected": "docs/implementation/m2/stage-meta-reference-selection-v1/successor.json", "sha256": "129bceca5f8e27cf3e14377453f8688b4169dd7b65aef1519f2bbdffc6880cb5"}, {"inputs": [{"bytes": 1010, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/native-runtime-selection-v13/README.md", "sha256": "0c0519a10979c4f8ca98edb8b28237aae65fe26331dce66d61870152f5b4cfa5"}, {"bytes": 179, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/native-runtime-selection-v13/evidence/archive-pin.json", "sha256": "24bcf0b88e5698293c07ebec5d54649d2a1f26b0c2896dcce46c2c39d7680b42"}, {"bytes": 40045, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/nativ