5060683d"}, {"bytes": 1999, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner-checkpoint-379/README.md", "sha256": "f05be628a02859600fa0c175a07d339383c6b8f33cd0ea93f36b871b262da200"}, {"bytes": 197, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner-checkpoint-379/archive-pin.json", "sha256": "e6943f6ba0074a6ef78b4feeb42afbd19933f8382906b7169b098f3f5a86b5e7"}, {"bytes": 20782, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner-checkpoint-379/subject.json", "sha256": "b2d76519241c1bb9275a9fb9e0bdc26d2f0054577b490b458ff0f881aedb02e3"}, {"bytes": 24504, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner-checkpoint-379/subject.tar.xz", "sha256": "1a9539613e0e811fa8e274213cb639dd3b13ca4332e9feaca7d83d96d27792e0"}, {"bytes": 356, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner-checkpoint-381-r2/COUNT-CORRECTION.md", "sha256": "333a5023f19b8d59388d6c5f0dcd9fcd30fdedec4e4fe77006fa15c86d42d658"}, {"bytes": 2281, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner-checkpoint-381-r2/README.md", "sha256": "12eb3530a2bf033db8c6108102ecc371b8833b94d318b5f73cf3c79ed87b9543"}, {"bytes": 200, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner-checkpoint-381-r2/archive-pin.json", "sha256": "66a12725fad49c2b02fd3a3dda3e294a8381e1fe0898f3cfdbe3e7b0a7d85265"}, {"bytes": 10283, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner-checkpoint-381-r2/subject.json", "sha256": "f725a9cd73ce12ec9a5781551ec78a4e5e4d49468c8f6a447a154ef18adabd01"}, {"bytes": 34384, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner-checkpoint-381-r2/subject.tar.xz", "sha256": "6f1548a51cffac0003b51ef14d1e5256ef66e931e32a85dc4fca60077831c03f"}, {"bytes": 1320, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner379-primary/README.md", "sha256": "08e712a5add80d2616d891f9b3ce3961c1ce8b30ab5a849b2e186161201a0956"}, {"bytes": 383, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/trials/project-registry-owner379-primary/source-pin.json", "sha256": "04ff6a31b29b82d74bacc53ad76956732bf0aa6b7f76747b27d5b21676a8d795"}], "passageOverrides": [{"after": "# Native ProjectId registry v2 \u2014 persistent root identity owner381", "before": "# Native ProjectId registry owner371 \u2014 working proposal", "parent": {"bytes": 27933, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v1/owner.md", "sha256": "14181ef7abadefc83391b45be013400a9680f2aac6222e35d257ef4e82359c8c"}, "selector": {"line": 1}}, {"after": "Proposed exact successor to selected registry371. Effectiveness requires independent review, root assent and an explicit selected design unit. This document alone authorizes no native writer, profile qualification, initialization, migration or public command. Historical v1 evidence stays immutable.", "before": "DRAFT. Not selected, frozen or accepted. No native writer is authorized by this document. This is a concrete proposed successor for the registry bridge identified by actual Grok370. Historical records keep their exact bytes. The final frozen unit must bind all source pins, semantic checks and independent review.", "parent": {"bytes": 27933, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v1/owner.md", "sha256": "14181ef7abadefc83391b45be013400a9680f2aac6222e35d257ef4e82359c8c"}, "selector": {"line": 3}}, {"after": "The sole current registry is `I/project-registry.v2`, relative to the admitted installation-root descriptor under the lifecycle fence. The former `I/project-registry.v1` name must be positively absent under that same original parent before ordinary v2 admission or authorized pristine v2 creation. A present or inaccessible v1 name, both names, or missing v2 in an established installation is unavailable/unsupported through the existing enclosing error owner, never permission to initialize, delete, rename or silently migrate. Neither absence alone proves pristine installation. The historical `lifecycle.sqlite` ProjectId-registry locator stays superseded for this role; journal/ledger SQLite owners are unchanged. No duplicated authoritative row lives in SQLite or a cache.", "before": "The sole registry is `I/project-registry.v1`, relative to the admitted installation-root descriptor under the lifecycle fence. The proposed `lifecycle.sqlite` ProjectId-registry locator is superseded for this role only; journal/ledger SQLite owners are unchanged. No duplicated authoritative registry row lives in SQLite or a cache.", "parent": {"bytes": 27933, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v1/owner.md", "sha256": "14181ef7abadefc83391b45be013400a9680f2aac6222e35d257ef4e82359c8c"}, "selector": {"line": 13}}, {"after": "Closed envelope: `{schemaVersion:2, entries:[Entry...]}`. Entries are strictly increasing by namespaceId's raw ASCII bytes. Each closed Entry has exactly:", "before": "Closed envelope: `{schemaVersion:1, entries:[Entry...]}`. Entries are strictly increasing by namespaceId's raw ASCII bytes. Each closed Entry has exactly:", "parent": {"bytes": 27933, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v1/owner.md", "sha256": "14181ef7abadefc83391b45be013400a9680f2aac6222e35d257ef4e82359c8c"}, "selector": {"line": 17}}, {"after": "- `root`: the closed NativeProjectRootV2 below.", "before": "- `root`: the closed NativeProjectRootV1 below.", "parent": {"bytes": 27933, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v1/owner.md", "sha256": "14181ef7abadefc83391b45be013400a9680f2aac6222e35d257ef4e82359c8c"}, "selector": {"line": 21}}, {"after": "NativeProjectRootV2 has exactly `platform`, `canonicalPathBytesHex`, `volumeIdentity`, `inodeId`, `birthSeconds`, `birthNanoseconds`. The initially specified persistent profile admits platform `macos` only. Native paths are raw POSIX bytes encoded as even-length lowercase hex: absolute,1..4096 bytes, no NUL, repeated separator, trailing separator except `/`, or `.`/`..` component. They must come from complete selected native root admission, never a caller path supplied as proof. VolumeIdentity is exactly `{kind,value}`: kind `macos-apfs-volume-uuid-v1`, value32 lowercase hexadecimal digits encoding sixteen native UUID bytes in order, nonzero. Unknown kind/platform, absent/malformed UUID or unsupported native acquisition is unavailable; there is no device/fsid/marker fallback. Other platforms need a separately specified and selected versioned kind, not an invented generic UUID interpretation.", "before": "NativeProjectRootV1 has exactly `platform`, `canonicalPathBytesHex`, `deviceId`, `inodeId`, `birthSeconds`, `birthNanoseconds`. Platform is `macos` or `linux`; native paths are raw POSIX bytes encoded as even-length lowercase hex. Decoded path is absolute, 1..4096 bytes, with no NUL, repeated separator, trailing separator except `/`, or `.`/`..` component. These are native path bytes, not UTF-8 repository paths or a source of authority. The path must be obtained and checked through the selected native root admission, never supplied as proof by a request.", "parent": {"bytes": 27933, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v1/owner.md", "sha256": "14181ef7abadefc83391b45be013400a9680f2aac6222e35d257ef4e82359c8c"}, "selector": {"line": 25}}, {"after": "Inode is a shortest unsigned decimal string in0..18446744073709551615 (no sign or leading zero except `0`). Birth seconds is an integer in signed64 range; nanoseconds integer0..999999999. macOS uses the original retained directory descriptor's inode, native birth and the independently qualified direct-descriptor APFS volume UUID. Missing reliable birth/UUID/profile is unavailable for reuse AND first-use without creating anything; no mtime/ctime/device/fsid/marker substitute. Raw device and mounted filesystem ID remain mandatory LIVE intra-operation observations and consistency checks, but do not enter the durable JSON key. Linux native registry use remains unavailable until a genuine descriptor-native persistent-volume/birth profile and versioned encoding are independently specified, implemented and qualified. A matching fixture or inert sampler does not qualify an OS/filesystem.", "before": "Device and inode are shortest unsigned decimal strings in0..18446744073709551615 (no sign or leading zero except `0`). Birth seconds is an integer in signed64 range; nanoseconds integer0..999999999. macOS uses the retained directory descriptor's device, inode and native birth time. Linux uses the retained descriptor's statx identity with STATX_BTIME present and canonical Linux device encoding. Missing reliable birth identity is unavailable, with no mtime/ctime/marker fallback. This is an explicit new native qualification gate, not a claim that identity \u00a72 itself already required birth-nanosecond metadata. In particular missing Linux STATX_BTIME refuses ordinary reuse AND first-use without creating anything. These requirements need native implementation and platform qualification; a fixture's matching numbers establish neither.", "parent": {"bytes": 27933, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v1/owner.md", "sha256": "14181ef7abadefc83391b45be013400a9680f2aac6222e35d257ef4e82359c8c"}, "selector": {"line": 27}}, {"after": "Every namespaceId is unique across ALL entries forever within this registry history. RESERVED and ACTIVE entries have mutually unique projectId, locator `(platform,canonicalPathBytesHex)` and, separately, durable native incarnation `(platform,volumeIdentity.kind,volumeIdentity.value,inodeId,birthSeconds,birthNanoseconds)`. Do not include pathname in the incarnation uniqueness key. Terminal rows may repeat historical ProjectIds/root locators but never namespaceId; terminal rows admit no current access. Identity \u00a72's one-to-one law remains LIVE ProjectId\u2194namespace uniqueness; explicit fresh-N adoption may retain retired historical ProjectId\u2194old-N records. N is never reused. All-zero ProjectId grammar remains valid and allocation still requires actual OS randomness.", "before": "Every namespaceId is unique across ALL entries forever within this registry history. RESERVED and ACTIVE entries have mutually unique projectId, `(platform,canonicalPathBytesHex)` and native incarnation `(platform,deviceId,inodeId,birthSeconds,birthNanoseconds)`. Terminal rows may repeat historical ProjectIds/root locators but never namespaceId. No terminal row admits current access. This successor explicitly resolves identity \u00a72's one-to-one law as LIVE ProjectId\u2194namespace uniqueness, not a prohibition on retaining a retired historical ProjectId\u2194old-N record after explicitly authorized fresh-N adoption. N itself is never reused across history. No empty/all-zero ProjectId spelling is treated specially: the grammar admits it; allocation still requires real OS randomness.", "parent": {"bytes": 27933, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v1/owner.md", "sha256": "14181ef7abadefc83391b45be013400a9680f2aac6222e35d257ef4e82359c8c"}, "selector": {"line": 29}}, {"after": "| Inaccessible root/registry/marker or old-v1 name, failed custody, unsupported volume/birth/profile, malformed/oversized registry or marker | unavailable or malformed evidence; never observed absence |", "before": "| Inaccessible root/registry/marker, failed custody, unsupported birth identity, malformed/oversized registry or marker | unavailable or malformed evidence; never observed absence |", "parent": {"bytes": 27933, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v1/owner.md", "sha256": "14181ef7abadefc83391b45be013400a9680f2aac6222e35d257ef4e82359c8c"}, "selector": {"line": 44}}, {"after": "Native registry v2 uses the qualified durable volume identity, inode and native birth at the admitted root, while retaining live descriptor device/filesystem-ID consistency. The sole current carrier is I/project-registry.v2; old project-registry.v1 presence or unavailable old-name evidence refuses and never silently migrates. Complete live locator and incarnation uniqueness are separate. Unchanged durable identity across operations may reuse without a write; same-present-path changed durable identity does not authorize rebind. The selected registry-v2 owner defines the initial macOS APFS kind, unsupported-profile refusal and coherent-copy limitation. Existing S7/S9 namespace projections and lock rules remain unchanged; S9.3 is not selected by this paragraph.", "before": "", "parent": {"bytes": 135448, "path": "docs/v2/contracts/product-v1/identity-and-evidence.md", "sha256": "c82404f3a0cf56fa6cc02e99cc3ebbd5356fedc3b36aeb38f9ef284077fbd31f"}, "selector": {"line": 52}}], "passageSupersessions": [], "selected": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v2/successor.json", "sha256": "cf91319a7e83c339000895e11460c3168436d67e5bd35a29289a2f5d87674f04"}, {"inputs": [{"bytes": 2493, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/native-runtime-selection-v28/README.md", "sha256": "657c7e0e051404b3cf4c80bbfc6fbfcfbc3b96305a983128bad7f30e450507db"}, {"bytes": 106108, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/native-runtime-selection-v28/baseline.json", "sha256": "6c31d6e90623949f7aeb0a5c5530a100ba21f4493e1b1302daff7067c3cfd7a8"}, {"bytes": 389, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/native-runtime-selection-v28/evidence/stage-command.json", "sha256": "4f446779c4096fab286428963ca07de814803eef51080844d1b3f1376ba8a38b"}, {"bytes": 0, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/native-runtime-selection-v28/evidence/stage.stderr", "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, {"bytes": 235, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/native-runtime-selection-v28/evidence/stage.stdout", "sha256": "18d8696c4dba28e2f46b2c9afac624e948b252fe428285cfab00808127db1bdf"}, {"bytes": 107502, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/native-runtime-selection-v28/materialization-map.json", "sha256": "ff05d1c2fe564b5f55d72bb83cf4dcff64e5b4628277aee10a7628549eec5a87"}, {"bytes": 5719, "path": "docs/implementa