 "86f0369bee55f8a892d3a4ad9679c2147a91a59fdd531a077450c0cd7ab25f70"}, {"bytes": 64953, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/schemas/common.v4.schema.json", "sha256": "19da184594e56dccabf0da1c9a1ecb06fff741860c28c04560aa04a09bf4ed8e"}, {"bytes": 3542, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/stage.py", "sha256": "69ba4cac36680c04956c6f3c529c0247b56a44d838c87979b776824e32b67749"}], "passageOverrides": [{"after": "| operation (`analyze`, `install`, `remove`, `update-index`, trust refresh) | open-then-verify of every executed or loaded closure member on its opened fd (the core itself and the component binaries about to run), not an eager hash of the whole inventory | decision evaluation with write-ahead `evalHighWater` (\u00a74.2) | yes, under \u00a75.6 | \u2014 |\n\nThe creator-only pre-installation sequence in docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md is an explicit exception to dependence on a pre-existing I/fence/current capsule: it authenticates original account/core/profile/embedded provenance before effects and publishes unbootstrapped P0 with unevaluated clock. It grants no ordinary role standing, time admission or requested analysis permission; those still require ordinary admission afterwards.", "before": "| operation (`analyze`, `install`, `remove`, `update-index`, trust refresh) | open-then-verify of every executed or loaded closure member on its opened fd (the core itself and the component binaries about to run), not an eager hash of the whole inventory | decision evaluation with write-ahead `evalHighWater` (\u00a74.2) | yes, under \u00a75.6 | \u2014 |", "parent": {"bytes": 69988, "path": "docs/coop/completion/security-completion.v8.md", "sha256": "54f3a6901d4192c5b6af82d4aad4414a84ee3b7748aa67cae06272a481e38c2d"}, "selector": {"line": 198}}, {"after": "journal append, quarantine marker, SC-TRUST high-water copy, lifecycle publication, selection commit. Additional initial-root boundaries are H confirmation; each fixed/staged directory and containing parent; final exclusive-rename I-parent confirmation; and existing-root I-directory/I-parent confirmation for writes. Their exact ordering, original observations and one act-wide budget are owned by docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md. Metadata/doctor/observation-only surfaces gain no barrier permission. Existing selected primitive and typed uncertainty rules remain.", "before": "journal append, quarantine marker, SC-TRUST high-water copy, lifecycle publication, selection commit.", "parent": {"bytes": 69988, "path": "docs/coop/completion/security-completion.v8.md", "sha256": "54f3a6901d4192c5b6af82d4aad4414a84ee3b7748aa67cae06272a481e38c2d"}, "selector": {"line": 322}}, {"after": "`doctor.defectsFound`. Only an unproducible report is `HOST.IO_FAILURE` (4), with detail `DOCTOR.REPORT_NOT_PRODUCIBLE`. For an observed complete I, the native doctor assembler adds one registered INSTALLATION.DURABILITY_NOT_CHECKED informational detail. Only that code is excluded from numeric defectsFound and DOCTOR.DEFECTS_FOUND selection. Capacity is255 actual defects plus the notice;256 actual defects refuse and latch instead of truncation. The result/count/goldens and current registry must activate together. Trust doctor/store status add no notice/channel. See docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md.", "before": "`doctor.defectsFound`. Only an unproducible report is `HOST.IO_FAILURE` (4), with detail `DOCTOR.REPORT_NOT_PRODUCIBLE`.", "parent": {"bytes": 139497, "path": "docs/implementation/m1/source-selection-v2/reference/effective-workflows-and-surfaces.md", "sha256": "4478ce1a69369cd0b430fd5d3fc695e8372219629b05a08ae6642a845cab794d"}, "selector": {"line": 1300}}, {"after": "This owner introduces private registry encoding and internal observation kinds only. It adds no public command, wire field, semantic identity input, signature domain, role state or public error code. Existing operation owners must supply authorization for installation, first-write, explicit recovery, move, fork, adoption and retirement. Their absence is not permission to invent a CLI surface or initialize on an ordinary read. The separately reviewed initial-root-binding owner supplies only initial installation publication and ordinary selected-store binding; its positive creator predicate, fixed-root storage choice, read/write split, bounded original-owner sequence and complete P0 publication are mandatory. Other recovery/move/fork/adoption/retirement owners remain separate. See docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md.", "before": "This owner introduces private registry encoding and internal observation kinds only. It adds no public command, wire field, semantic identity input, signature domain, role state or public error code. Existing operation owners must supply authorization for installation, first-write, explicit recovery, move, fork, adoption and retirement. Their absence is not permission to invent a CLI surface or initialize on an ordinary read.", "parent": {"bytes": 32488, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v2/owner.md", "sha256": "2d4b65c9b0bc088b2667c35e75bf82d1702d13703be6effb1df975e7c67c179f"}, "selector": {"line": 9}}, {"after": "Proposed dynamic native installation placement; not a repository source-file inventory; installation-root location and complete initial staged tree are governed by docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md without replacing the registry/namespace paths here.", "before": "Proposed dynamic native installation placement; not a repository source-file inventory", "parent": {"bytes": 1328, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v2/physical-placement.json", "sha256": "ac65782333759b9ae03a2cd772f5763dda4a6e88e92f36b7dc199c599559b4b3"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/standing"}}, {"after": "Retain the selected pair, every immutable lineage node and the physically opened selected endpoint store marker under the ordinary binding owner. Admit complete node ancestry without requiring reclaimed intermediate physical stores; recheck all contributing original descriptors and latch failures under one operation budget. Separate observation-only from durable/write capabilities; structural values alone grant no namespace/current authority.", "before": "Retain the selected pair, every lineage node and each corresponding store marker under one native installation fence; recheck every contributing descriptor before consumption and latch failures. Provisional structural evidence only; namespace, operation-wide budget, transition authorization and full binding remain separate.", "parent": {"bytes": 280949, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v59.json", "sha256": "c2400990cf4f9ec0c6c4e4331e2194313dea272f17ad04c83866a23c9c1cb815"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/104/description"}}, {"after": "Author correction for review finding PS-01, revision 5. Proposed minimal successor delta to the security S9 owner plus its private lifecycle companion. Not an accepted amendment, not executable product code, not a wire schema and not acceptance of frozen candidate25 bytes. Requires its own substantive review on newly frozen bytes. Initial/ordinary native binding is now separately specified in docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md; it preserves these private shapes/digest recipes while requiring physical markers only at opened endpoints and retained immutable nodes for intermediate ancestry. This does not adopt this historical transition/recovery/restore proposal.", "before": "Author correction for review finding PS-01, revision 5. Proposed minimal successor delta to the security S9 owner plus its private lifecycle companion. Not an accepted amendment, not executable product code, not a wire schema and not acceptance of frozen candidate25 bytes. Requires its own substantive review on newly frozen bytes.", "parent": {"bytes": 68487, "path": "docs/v2/architecture/store-instance-lineage.v1.json", "sha256": "919d1717b53f202b2e53a4f580b7f3df13f908b3575d4a97ad22e7bc6f185210"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/standing"}}, {"after": "write, also identifying the actual account-derived operational storage root; the command's documented effect is admission of the project marker and", "before": "write; the command's documented effect is admission of the project marker and", "parent": {"bytes": 135448, "path": "docs/v2/contracts/product-v1/identity-and-evidence.md", "sha256": "c82404f3a0cf56fa6cc02e99cc3ebbd5356fedc3b36aeb38f9ef284077fbd31f"}, "selector": {"line": 1635}}, {"after": "a backup acknowledgement is not a network-export or shared-storage grant. For first creation under docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md, the account-derived root is fixed and there is no outside-I policy record: BACKED_UP requires this invocation's explicit --allow-backup-custody before any fixed ancestor/stage effect, or an explicitly selected separate ephemeral route where supported. The alternative-root/already-admitted-policy remedies above do not apply before I exists; UNKNOWN retains disclosure.", "before": "a backup acknowledgement is not a network-export or shared-storage grant.", "parent": {"bytes": 135448, "path": "docs/v2/contracts/product-v1/identity-and-evidence.md", "sha256": "c82404f3a0cf56fa6cc02e99cc3ebbd5356fedc3b36aeb38f9ef284077fbd31f"}, "selector": {"line": 1655}}, {"after": "### S9.3 Historical proposed lineage companion; initial/ordinary binding has a separate selected owner\n\nOnly the independently specified initial-publication and ordinary-binding law in docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md is selected by that unit. This section remains historical proposed transition/recovery law except for the explicitly scoped endpoint lookup clarification below. No transition writer, restore, reconstruction or broad S9.3 adoption follows.", "before": "### S9.3 Private store-instance lineage (successor; proposed, not accepted)", "parent": {"bytes": 119915, "path": "docs/v2/contracts/product-v1/security-and-lifecycle.md", "sha256": "a319da39b9f90aff4483a295af3fe004540c71861fb2bd34e84c7e1318bad9d6"}, "selector": {"line": 953}}, {"after": "comes from a real store-root **marker** at a physically opened endpoint; for ordinary ancestry traversal under docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md, intermediate immutable node keys suffice and reclaimed intermediate physical stores/markers are not required. A numeric pair alone", "before": "is read from the store-root **marker** of the store concerned: a numeric pair alone", "parent": {"bytes": 119915, "path": "docs/v2/contracts/product-v1/security-and-lifecycle.md", "sha256": "a319da39b9f90aff4483a295af3fe004540c71861fb2bd34e84c7e1318bad9d6"}, "selector": {"line": 977}}, {"after": "`doctor.defectsFound`. Only an unproducible report is `HOST.IO_FAILURE` (4), with detail `DOCTOR.REPORT_NOT_PRODUCIBLE`. For an observed complete I, the native doctor assembler adds one registered INSTALLATION.DURABILITY_NOT_CHECKED informational detail. Only that code is excluded from numeric defectsFound and DOCTOR.DEFECTS_FOUND selection. Capacity is255 actual defects plus the notice;256 actual defects refuse and latch instead of truncation. The result/count/goldens and current registry must activate together. Trust doctor/store status add no notice/channel. See docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md.", "before": "`doctor.defectsFound`. Only an unproducible report is `HOST.IO_FAILURE` (4), with detail `DOCTOR.REPORT_NOT_PRODUCIBLE`.", "parent": {"bytes": 133335, "path": "docs/v2/contracts/product-v1/workflows-and-surfaces.md", "sha256": "1ee203e3ce626d88a53d0247881cd3ffb0d52b421821ac798b9f0b57346ff6ed"}