ach refusal names its item 8 row; the public projection is the composition owner's. A cfg(test) seam stops at each step and scripts candidate draws. Library only: no lease (X2d) and no handoff (X2e).", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/381/description"}}, {"after": "Check doctor's installation check on scratch account homes with a creator-published P0: a complete installation with the fence released; every missing member its own finding in member order; an undecodable pair, marker or node, and a missing node, as their findings; and a missing home, a fence busy through the wait, and a member refused custody each ending on its row with no report. It also checks the security layer's part of law X10 item 5: a node from another store's lineage as the chain finding, and an account refusal, no premise, an exhausted session ledger and a positively absent I ending on the account, omitted-ACL custody, budget and not-initialized rows; and an undecodable trust current record, or one still naming G 0 after the pair is reselected at G 1, as the current-store finding (law X3a item 5, unit X3a-1).", "before": "Check doctor's installation check on scratch account homes with a creator-published P0: a complete installation with the fence released; every missing member its own finding in member order; an undecodable pair, marker or node, and a missing node, as their findings; and a missing home, a fence busy through the wait, and a member refused custody each ending on its row with no report.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/389/description"}}, {"after": "Resolve the fixed installation root from the actual account database and retain its existing or missing-path evidence; do not derive authority from environment variables. It also holds the creator's read half of owner \u00a71a step 5 (law 460): observe_installation_parent, on the attempt's one ledger with that attempt's actor and premise, retains and judges root to H and then each existing fixed ancestor (Library, Application Support, OpenSIP) with charged opens, ACL captures and name checks, and reports a missing ancestor, preview-v1 positively absent through the retained OpenSIP, or preview-v1 present; every directory through Application Support must pass the external ancestor check, an omitted ACL only through InitialPlatform's Evidence B premise, OpenSIP must be private, names and the actor are rechecked at the end, any refusal latches the attempt, and nothing is created. That walk (observe_parent, which law 465's preparation runs with OpenSIP retained by name only), the external ancestor judgment of one capture (judge_ancestor, judge_captured_ancestor) and the ParentRefusal rows are shared by the parent preparation, the durable write gate's chain walk and recheck, and the project chain walk. A cfg(test) per-thread record of each capture judge_ancestor refused as changed is what F5's churned reads.", "before": "Resolve the fixed installation root from the actual account database and retain its existing or missing-path evidence; do not derive authority from environment variables.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/398/description"}}, {"after": "Check the observation path on scratch account homes, with P0 published by the creator composition and the read receipt built from signed on-disk test trees, and an injected wait clock: a complete I observed under the fence with no barrier; positive absence at each suffix component, and a symlink, a file or a custody refusal at a suffix name not taken for absence; a missing H on the write gate's row; no premise refusing at the root; a busy fence retried on the same descriptor to 5 s or 201 attempts, freed during the wait, or ending on a wait error; the wait reserved before its first attempt; a required file's mode, link count or identity changed before the final recheck; every finding of an incomplete I; a deep home well within the caps; a failed member capture after which the final recheck still runs and the capture failure stays the reported cause; and no ordinary fence acquire in the source. It also checks law X3a's one read (unit X3a-1): a complete observation retaining the endpoint values of its one read and every required file's full sample; an undecodable or oversized trust current record as the current-store finding with no endpoint values, every read but doctor's ending on the incomplete row; a node chain past the session limit, or unended after 64 nodes at G 63, on the budget row as an ordinary failure, not a finding; and a 64-node chain on a deep home read once within the owner's caps, its trust current record still naming G 0 as the current-store finding.", "before": "Check the observation path on scratch account homes, with P0 published by the creator composition and the read receipt built from signed on-disk test trees, and an injected wait clock: a complete I observed under the fence with no barrier; positive absence at each suffix component, and a symlink, a file or a custody refusal at a suffix name not taken for absence; a missing H on the write gate's row; no premise refusing at the root; a busy fence retried on the same descriptor to 5 s or 201 attempts, freed during the wait, or ending on a wait error; the wait reserved before its first attempt; a required file's mode, link count or identity changed before the final recheck; every finding of an incomplete I; a deep home well within the caps; and no ordinary fence acquire in the source.", "parent": {"bytes": 55217