701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/412/description"}}, {"after": "Dispatch observed carrier schema names and exact definitions within one read-only SQLite snapshot; historical classification does not authorize migration or repair. The captured dispatch also reports whether its snapshot holds an inherited format-1 or format-2 grant_journal beside or instead of the current objects (inherited_present), which X6a's read-only recovery capture uses to tell the lawful {A, B} migration prefix from an unpublished fresh footprint (law X6 r2 item 1, unit X6a).", "before": "Dispatch observed carrier schema names and exact definitions within one read-only SQLite snapshot; historical classification does not authorize migration or repair.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/440/description"}}, {"after": "The grant journal's half of the operation handoff (law X3b r10 items 1, 3, 3a, 4 and 11; unit X3b-3, composed with X2e): the carrier location's writer-side production constructor, which takes only the carrier place X2e's handoff confirms (recovery_location.rs holds the recovery side's, unit X6b); the floor step at X2's lease-free point, keeping the committed tail the start must confirm; inside the handoff under the fence and the writer lease, item 3a's creation when the floor step found INIT, item 4's carrier start against that observation and item 6's append lock from it, with a skipped floor step (busy writer.lease) refusing on the busy row if the lease was nevertheless taken; and the end step's probe, read and forward-only floor copy after certain outcomes, or, after a capacity exhaustion, the end step from its step 3 (X3b-4's rollover, then the copy). It adds no carrier semantics and composes only X3b-1's, X3b-2's and X3b-4's steps. It also passes on the append surface others name through journal_store: JournalAppendHeld, the level-4 borrow X4's checkpoint receives (law X4 r7 item 3, unit X4a), and, for X3d-1's commit session, the end path's records, the append outcome, the detached level 3 and the end path's exact cost and body bounds. Under cfg(test) or the test-only crash-matrix feature only, one helper plants a committed tail with X3b-2's reserved-slot technique (also for the composition owner's and the commit session's tests) and another an inherited format-1 or format-2 carrier (InheritedFormat): the crash matrix's carrier fixtures (law X9 r1 item 6, unit X9-1); cfg(test) re-exports carry X3b-2's append test points and X3b-4's rollover test points, and a cfg(test) seam lends the started lock to install an append hook (unit X3d-1). Library only.", "before": "The grant journal's half of the operation handoff (law X3b r10 items 1, 3, 3a, 4 and 11; unit X3b-3, composed with X2e): the carrier location's production constructor, which takes only the carrier place X2e's handoff confirms; the floor step at X2's lease-free point, keeping the committed tail the start must confirm; inside the handoff under the fence and the writer lease, item 3a's creation when the floor step found INIT, item 4's carrier start against that observation and item 6's append lock from it, with a skipped floor step (busy writer.lease) refusing on the busy row if the lease was nevertheless taken; and the end step's probe, read and forward-only floor copy after certain outcomes, or, after a capacity exhaustion, the end step from its step 3 (X3b-4's rollover, then the copy). It adds no carrier semantics and composes only X3b-1's, X3b-2's and X3b-4's steps. A cfg(test) helper plants a committed tail with X3b-2's reserved-slot technique, and cfg(test) re-exports carry X3b-4's rollover test points, for the composition owner's tests. Library only.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/443/description"}}, {"after": "Grant-generation rollover (law X3b r10 item 13, with items 4a, 5, 5a, 8 and 9; unit X3b-4), as carrier_floor.rs's macOS child module rollover, and the end step's exhaustion input (item 4 step 3). end_step_after_exhaustion takes X3d's CarrierCapacityExhausted {grantGeneration, provenTailSeq} and the released operation's operationRef, runs the rollover, then X3b-1b's floor copy (steps 4 and 5), which after an undetermined rollover copies nothing and is not entered on an attempt ledger the rollover closed (r10); the composition owner holds the fence around it with no project lock held. The rollover refuses an input on which a SEAL still fits (seal_fits) as a broken composition, then makes one fixed reservation on the attempt ledger before any lease (leases, classification with the predecessor and tail queries, witness and floor reads, the entropy draw and clock sample, step 3's one REVERT or ADVANCE witness write, one TERMINAL append at item 5's cost, and OPEN's witness write); a failed reservation takes no lease. It takes EXCLUSIVE as writer.lease then readers.lease LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB, never waiting, and on either busy releases what it took and returns Skipped. Under the lease it observes the carrier start's state (classification, binding, predecessor check, the committed tail, the witness) and the floor (with item 4a's open-successor exception), and decides by item 13's table in order: any quarantine or floor regression refuses; a later generation or an open successor is AlreadyRolled; a closing TERMINAL the witness names OK or ADVANCE is OPEN only; an open generation 9223372036854775807 refuses on the invariant row; a tail below the proven tail refuses as floor regression or uncertainTailLoss; an open in-window tail at or above the proof closes. Closing mints the TERMINAL's operationRef (op- and 16 host-CSPRNG bytes as hex, once per attempt, never the released operation's, no redraw) and one UTC clock sample in the frozen YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ shape before any write, writes a REVERT or ADVANCE witness as the start does, makes its own JournalAppendLock, appends the TERMINAL with cause grantGenerationClosure through item 5 inside item 5a's window, then OPENs G+1 by the witness COMMITTED (G+1, 0, null) alone, drops the lock, and releases readers.lease then writer.lease. It writes no floor (the end step's copy writes (G+1, 0, null) after the lease is released), no carrier row but the TERMINAL, and no carrier_capacity_pause or quarantine row. After a failure after visibility nothing follows in the operation (no reconciliation, carrier read, witness write or floor copy; r9 item 5): the lock is dropped, the lease released, and the outcome disclosed as DURABILITY.COMMIT_FAILED, leaving a crash-table state the next writer's floor step and start reconcile. Decision refusals leave the attempt ledger open for the end step's copy. Outcomes are Skipped, AlreadyRolled, Rolled, Refused and Undetermined, each with item 8's row. Its own crash and fault hooks, and injectable entropy and clock, exist only under cfg(test); law X9's barrier points (law X9 r1 item 5, unit X9-1) exist only under the test-only crash-matrix feature: the x3b.rollover scope with a point at each RolloverStep place and scopes around the lease takes and releases and the witness writes, the TERMINAL append's x3b.append.terminal and the end step's x3b.end.floor; without the feature a point compiles to nothing and a scope to the code it wraps. Library only.", "before": "Grant-generation rollover (law X3b r10 item 13, with items 4a, 5, 5a, 8 and 9; unit X3b-4), as carrier_floor.rs's macOS child module rollover, and the end step's exhaustion input (item 4 step 3). end_step_after_exhaustion takes X3d's CarrierCapacityExhausted {grantGeneration, provenTailSeq} and the released operation's operationRef, runs the rollover, then X3b-1b's floor copy (steps 4 and 5), which after an undetermined rollover copies nothing and is not entered on an attempt ledger the rollover closed (r10); the composition owner holds the fence around it with no project lock held. The rollover refuses an input on which a SEAL still fits (seal_fits) as a broken composition, then makes one fixed reservation on the attempt ledger before any lease (leases, classification with the predecessor and tail queries, witness and floor reads, the entropy draw and clock sample, step 3's one REVERT or ADVANCE witness write, one TERMINAL append at item 5's cost, and OPEN's witness write); a failed reservation takes no lease. It takes EXCLUSIVE as writer.lease then readers.lease LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB, never waiting, and on either busy releases what it took and returns Skipped. Under the lease it observes the carrier start's state (classification, binding, predecessor check, the committed tail, the witness) and the floor (with item 4a's open-successor exception), and decides by item 13's table in order: any quarantine or floor regression refuses; a later generation or an open successor is AlreadyRolled; a closing TERMINAL the witness names OK or ADVANCE is OPEN only; an open generation 9223372036854775807 refuses on the invariant row; a tail below the proven tail refuses as floor regression or uncertainTailLoss; an open in-window tail at or above the proof closes. Closing mints the TERMINAL's operationRef (op- and 16 host-CSPRNG bytes as hex, once per attempt, never the released operation's, no redraw) and one UTC clock sample in the frozen YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ shape before any write, writes a REVERT or ADVANCE witness as the start does, makes its own JournalAppendLock, appends the TERMINAL with cause grantGenerationClosure through item 5 inside item 5a's window, then OPENs G+1 by the witness COMMITTED (G+1, 0, null) alone, drops the lock, and releases readers.lease then writer.lease. It writes no floor (the end step's copy writes (G+1, 0, null) after the lease is released), no carrier row but the TERMINAL, and no carrier_capacity_pause or quarantine row. After a failure after visibility nothing follows in the operation (no reconciliation, carrier read, witness write or floor copy; r9 item 5): the lock is dropped, the lease released, and the outcome disclosed as DURABILITY.COMMIT_FAILED, leaving a crash-table state the next writer's floor step and start reconcile. Decision refusals leave the attempt ledger open for the end step's copy. Outcomes are Skipped, AlreadyRolled, Rolled, Refused and Undetermined, each with item 8's row. Crash and fault hooks, and injectable entropy and clock, exist only under cfg(test). Library only.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/445/description"}}, {"after": "Store-data custody for the per-project store directories and files (law X3c r6 items 1 and 2), under a supplied retained store directory and the caller's namespace writer lease, or, for read-only recovery's reads, its shared readers.lease (unit X6b). create_or_admit_store_directory applies 465 item 3: a charged exclusive 0700 create with the zero-rights owner allow, or, only on a raw EEXIST, a fresh no-follow admission of the existing entry judged private; then the exact name, the parent's filesystem, the directory's own barrier and its parent's barrier. A link or non-directory at the name is a kind refusal; an existing mode or ACL is never changed. create_store_file makes one private 0600 file exclusively after a no-follow absence sample, and open_store_file opens an existing regular file no-follow and judges it private. admit_existing_store_directory is read-only recovery's admission of an existing store directory (law X6 r3 item 4, unit X6b): nothing is created and no barrier is taken; the entry is opened no-follow if present, judged private, bound to its exact name and on its parent's filesystem, and a positively absent name is Ok(None), which the caller never reads as absence of history. Store data, not trust state; it selects no store, admits no namespace and grants nothing. Library only.", "before": "Store-data custody for the per-project store directories and files (law X3c r6 items 1 and 2), under a supplied retained store directory and the caller's namespace writer lease. create_or_admit_store_directory applies 465 item 3: a charged exclusive 0700 create with the zero-rights owner allow, or, only on a raw EEXIST, a fresh no-follow admission of the existing entry judged private; then the exact name, the parent's filesystem, the directory's own barrier and its parent's barrier. A link or non-directory at the name is a kind refusal; an existing mode or ACL is never changed. create_store_file makes one private 0600 file exclusively after a no-follow absence sample, and open_store_file opens an existing regular file no-follow and judges it private. Store data, not trust state; it selects no store, admits no namespace and grants nothing. Library only.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/466/description"}}, {"after": "Validate retained core inventory syntax, paths, DAG, semantic versions and bootstrap members before anchor authentication. From the bound descriptor it also derives the release's closure2: identity and its core evaluator closure (contract successor EC1, law X3d r8 item 13, unit X3d-3): closure2: over the same descriptor with kind set to evaluator and every other member unchanged (evaluator_descriptor), which InitialCore lends for a Run's evaluator closure check; its tests reproduce EC1's vector byte for byte and check every accepted core-inventory318 case.", "before": "Validate retained core inventory syntax, paths, DAG, semantic versions and bootstrap members before anchor authentication.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/488/description"}}, {"after": "Check the read-only current-trust admission over X4T-0's signed store: an accepted store is admitted for state schemas 1 and 2 with its epoch, empty-policy digest and install-gate standing; a creator-only capsule is F absent before any read; each continuation refusal names its role and state under CONTINUE-CORE-NOT-TRUSTED; an expired or stale index is admitted as existing-only; time is admitted only on the fenced read, report-only proposes no writes, and the payload-future, beyond-horizon and in-session refusals take their rows; the policy digest is equal on both reads; accepted.by must name a loaded event of that role; each member X4T-a opens is required; the measured view cost is pinned within TRUST_VIEW_COST; the event, chain and ledger bounds refuse on the budget row; a recorded rotation of one to three roots is admitted from its first root with heads.root as the signing root, at the final root's epoch and rootVersion floor on the fenced read and a reread; a closure rootChain ending on another envelope of the head or short is incomplete (FinalIdentity) and an empty one is refused by its shape; a first root below its own threshold, also once the list's keyIds are excluded, is not admissible; a failing link takes its S5 row (ROOT.CHAIN_OLD_THRESHOLD or ROOT.CHAIN_NEW_THRESHOLD) naming the link; a list signed under the signing root is admitted with its entries, and one signed only by root 1's keys is refused (law X4T r10 item 12 and, for the list, r11 item 4, unit X4T-a3); and the native read through a supplied fence admits the written store and refuses a replaced record.", "before": "Check the read-only current-trust admission over X4T-0's signed store: an accepted store is admitted for state schemas 1 and 2 with its epoch, empty-policy digest and install-gate standing; a creator-only capsule is F absent before any read; each continuation refusal names its role and state under CONTINUE-CORE-NOT-TRUSTED; an expired or stale index is admitted as existing-only; time is admitted only on the fenced read, report-only proposes no writes, and the payload-future, beyond-horizon and in-session refusals take their rows; the policy digest is equal on both reads; accepted.by must name a loaded event of that role; each member X4T-a opens is required; the measured view cost is pinned within TRUST_VIEW_COST; the event, chain and ledger bounds refuse on the budget row; and the native read through a supplied fence admits the written store and refuses a replaced record.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/493/description"}}, {"after": "Perform the fenced first read's S4 write-ahead floor publication (law X4T r9 items 7 and 8; unit X4T-b), as a child of the current-trust admission, under the installation fence with no project lock and before any lease. The retained trust current owner is the session's one read of trust/stores/S/state.v1 (its bytes, the capsule decoded from them and its full custody sample), with trust/stores/S bound by a metadata recheck, never a second content read; any change but a confirmed publication is required-files-changed. The read admits the owner's capsule through X4T-a, applies rollback check 3 against the floors of every evaluated or retained capsule this fence hold retained before (checks 1 and 2 run in every admission), and, unless report-only, publishes when F rises, L advances or the anchor changes: the before image, the S4EvaluationInputV2 from proposed_time_input's assembler, a host-trust-admission operation with its continue input for the running core, the clock-write event, the by-predecessor descriptor and the successor capsule with every other field unchanged, verified first by successor_record_bindings and current_record_bindings. The publication protocol, shared with X4B-a, reserves its writes and post-publication confirmation before the first effect (each exact reread at the platform's read_bounded_cost with the read session's attempt bound, so nothing is charged after the first effect), writes each dependency through the private-file producer with its file and directory barriers (admitting an existing record only when its bytes are equal), replaces state.v1 last through X3b's private file protocol, rereads and samples it, and advances the owner, minting ConfirmedCurrent for the gate's advance_current; the owner keeps every confirmed publication of its hold in order (confirmations, unit X4B-b). Nothing is retried or deleted; failures take the host I/O, budget, incomplete or custody rows. Beside it, publish_store_fenced is the shared fenced state.v1 publisher (law X9 r1 item 6, law X8 r3 items 4b and 5a; unit X9-1), declared only under the shared fixture gates' one joint predicate any(test, feature = crash-matrix, feature = scenario-fixtures) and with no production caller: under a held fence it binds the retained owner to the write gate's one read of state.v1, turns each generated file into its records, objects, events or publications write (refusing a path its locator does not give back exactly), and runs that protocol with state.v1 last, returning the ConfirmedCurrent; the shared installation fixture is its one caller. Library only.", "before": "Perform the fenced first read's S4 write-ahead floor publication (law X4T r9 items 7 and 8; unit X4T-b), as a child of the current-trust admission, under the installation fence with no project lock and before any lease. The retained trust current owner is the session's one read of trust/stores/S/state.v1 (its bytes, the capsule decoded from them and its full custody sample), with trust/stores/S bound by a metadata recheck, never a second content read; any change but a confirmed publication is required-files-changed. The read admits the owner's capsule through X4T-a, applies rollback check 3 against the floors of every evaluated or retained capsule this fence hold retained before (checks 1 and 2 run in every admission), and, unless report-only, publishes when F rises, L advances or the anchor changes: the before image, the S4EvaluationInputV2 from proposed_time_input's assembler, a host-trust-admission operation with its continue input for the running core, the clock-write event, the by-predecessor descriptor and the successor capsule with every other field unchanged, verified first by successor_record_bindings and current_record_bindings. The publication protocol, shared with X4B-a, reserves its writes and post-publication confirmation before the first effect (each exact reread at the platform's read_bounded_cost with the read session's attempt bound, so nothing is charged after the first effect), writes each dependency through the private-file producer with its file and directory barriers (admitting an existing record only when its bytes are equal), replaces state.v1 last through X3b's private file protocol, rereads and samples it, and advances the owner, minting ConfirmedCurrent for the gate's advance_current. Nothing is retried or deleted; failures take the host I/O, budget, incomplete or custody rows. Library only.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/500/description"}}, {"after": "Check X4T-a2 and X4T-b (law X4T r9 item 12) on ACL-scratch installations with X4T-0's signed store under a supplied fence: a floor advance is written ahead with F := tEval, the anchor rewritten and every other field, L and the time evidence unchanged, the descriptor in the predecessor's bucket, the pointer last and the retained owner advanced to the confirmed file; the next invocation's fenced read and the native reread admit the store with each accepted role's acceptance event opened by reference, at a pinned measured cost within TRUST_VIEW_COST; a floor publication on a store whose recorded chain rotates root 1 to root 2 keeps the heads and is followed by an admitted fenced read and native reread at root 2's epoch and rootVersion floor (law X4T r10 item 12, unit X4T-a3); accepted.by naming another role's event, a missing event, another store, a non-role event or the current chain's clock-write refuses as incomplete; a confirming admission on the same clock sample writes nothing; report-only and a beyond-horizon refusal write nothing; an in-place rewrite of state.v1 is required-files-changed; check 3 refuses below this hold's floors and an unevaluated predecessor is never compared; checks 1 and 2 over retained, evaluated and unevaluated before-clocks, the evaluation wall and an S4.5 epoch input; a whole-file restore of an older self-consistent state.v1 is admitted, pinning the stated limit; the protocol admits an equal content-addressed record and refuses a foreign one before the pointer; at each reread growth boundary up to the 131072-byte parser cap (16384, 20480, 32768, 53248, 65536, 118784, 131072) a publication beside an equal record of that length completes on an exactly sufficient ledger and refuses before any effect with one byte less; a short ledger writes nothing; and a reread mode is not a fenced first read. Compiled only for tests; confers no qualification.", "before": "Check X4T-a2 and X4T-b (law X4T r9 item 12) on ACL-scratch installations with X4T-0's signed store under a supplied fence: a floor advance is written ahead with F := tEval, the anchor rewritten and every other field, L and the time evidence unchanged, the descriptor in the predecessor's bucket, the pointer last and the retained owner advanced to the confirmed file; the next invocation's fenced read and the native reread admit the store with each accepted role's acceptance event opened by reference, at a pinned measured cost within TRUST_VIEW_COST; accepted.by naming another role's event, a missing event, another store, a non-role event or the current chain's clock-write refuses as incomplete; a confirming admission on the same clock sample writes nothing; report-only and a beyond-horizon refusal write nothing; an in-place rewrite of state.v1 is required-files-changed; check 3 refuses below this hold's floors and an unevaluated predecessor is never compared; checks 1 and 2 over retained, evaluated and unevaluated before-clocks, the evaluation wall and an S4.5 epoch input; a whole-file restore of an older self-consistent state.v1 is admitted, pinning the stated limit; the protocol admits an equal content-addressed record and refuses a foreign one before the pointer; at each reread growth boundary up to the 131072-byte parser cap (16384, 20480, 32768, 53248, 65536, 118784, 131072) a publication beside an equal record of that length completes on an exactly sufficient ledger and refuses before any effect with one byte less; a short ledger writes nothing; and a reread mode is not a fenced first read. Compiled only for tests; confers no qualification.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/501/description"}}, {"after": "Build a signed on-disk core tree with the public test-only quorum62 seeds and explicit ACLs, and check InitialCore end to end with an injected running-image observation and every refusal. It also holds InitialCore::evaluator_closure_preimages (law X3d r8 item 13, unit X3d-3), the read behind the shared test-support accessor for the synthetic run candidate: the core evaluator closure's descriptor (contract successor EC1), the TR-CORE-signed inventory body and each tree member's bytes by logical path, read through the core's retained tree root as a release file is judged and checked against the inventory's digest and length. Compiled for tests and, as shared fixture gate 1's module defining the injected image and the signed test tree, under the shared fixture gates' one joint predicate any(test, feature = crash-matrix, feature = scenario-fixtures) (law X8 r3 item 4b, unit X9-1), so absent from every release build; confers no release qualification.", "before": "Build a signed on-disk core tree with the public test-only quorum62 seeds and explicit ACLs, and check InitialCore end to end with an injected running-image observation and every refusal. Compiled only for tests; confers no release qualification.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/505/description"}}, {"after": "Sign SYNTHETIC profile sets at run time with the public test-only quorum62 seeds, including a V2 measured row built from this host's observed identity, and check InitialPlatform end to end over the signed on-disk core tree: both authentication paths, the tier, Evidence B and every refusal. It also provides the receipt producers: receipts_at (InitialCore and InitialPlatform on one attempt, for law 465's tests) and read_producers (for law 458c's read composition: InitialCore through the injected image of a signed test tree, and InitialPlatform with H at a chosen home, under PM with the premise or the BASELINE-ATTESTED P469 without one), which the crash-matrix and scenario support surfaces also hold. Compiled for tests and, as part of shared fixture gate 1 (the synthetic V2 profile set and its receipt producers), under the shared fixture gates' one joint predicate any(test, feature = crash-matrix, feature = scenario-fixtures) (law X8 r3 item 4b, unit X9-1), with F6's churn retry in the test build only; checks in no measured row and confers no qualification.", "before": "Sign SYNTHETIC profile sets at run time with the public test-only quorum62 seeds, including a V2 measured row built from this host's observed identity, and check InitialPlatform end to end over the signed on-disk core tree: both authentication paths, the tier, Evidence B and every refusal. Compiled only for tests; checks in no measured row and confers no qualification.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/507/description"}}, {"after": "Check X3d-2's storage half, included as commit.rs's cfg(test) module, on a scratch private I/stores/S under the per-process scratch parent, with binding values from a real session, never from the Run under test (law X3d r8 item 13, unit X3d-3): bound() takes the project and the core evaluator closure from a CommitSession opened once per process over X8b's scenario-fixtures ProjectOperation on a synthetic installation under the scratch parent, and the evaluator's real replay is of the synthetic run candidate built for that session (crash_matrix_support/run_candidate.rs, included by path): the plan declares exactly the retained typed objects (each frame its identity's H preimage, published under its H digest) and raw blobs, once each, and the commit inventory lists them; a Run of another project or another evaluator closure does not bind; the pinned corpus Run that security's SEAL tests replay, rebound to the session's project, is refused on its evaluator closure, and through prepare_commit on a real session on the invariant row with no namespace directory in the store and the end path's REV; the session's core closure is not its core evaluator closure, and a candidate renamed to name the core closure does not replay while one renamed to another evaluator closure does; the store generation digest is store-instance-lineage v1's recipe; a prepared commit publishes every frame and blob, stages the receipt (sequence 1, replayable, the unsigned local-custody signer), the thirteen-field association, the Run material, generation-0 retained availability and no pins with nothing visible to another connection until its one COMMIT, after which the pair joins the admitted attempt with settlement pending; the receipt counter orders stored canonical decimals by length then bytes (2, 9, 10, 100 give 101) and refuses a full u64 on the invariant row; a SEAL binding whose RunId, carrier digest or operationRef does not join stages nothing; an error from the evidence COMMIT is undetermined with the attempt still admitted; prepare_commit and publish compose end to end on a real session, the first real commit: Committed at sequence 1 and not latched, the end path appending no REV or CLN, the carrier holding one SEAL, and the store holding exactly the receipt, the attempt row still admitted and every retained frame and blob, the core evaluator closure's inventory body and tree included; the publication reserve equals exactly what attempt admission and the objects charge, and one byte short refuses on the budget row before the attempt row and any object; a reused ExecutionId is refused before any object; every ledger row maps to its existing termination; and x3d.publish.published is placed once, after the one PublishedCommit construction. Its child modules recover (recover_tests.rs, unit X6b) and settlement_sweep (sweep_tests.rs, unit X6c) run recovery's recover_from and the settlement sweep's sweep_from over the stores these steps commit.", "before": "Check X3d-2's storage half without a session (storage cannot build a CommitSession: security's fixtures are cfg(test) there and law X8 r3 item 4's scenario-fixtures seam is X8b's), on a scratch private I/stores/S under the per-process scratch parent, with the evaluator's real replay of the corpus Run that security's SEAL tests replay, included as commit.rs's cfg(test) module: the plan declares exactly the retained typed objects (each frame its identity's H preimage, published under its H digest) and raw blobs, once each, and the commit inventory lists them; a Run of another project or another evaluator closure does not bind; the store generation digest is store-instance-lineage v1's recipe; a prepared commit publishes every frame and blob, stages the receipt (sequence 1, replayable, the unsigned local-custody signer), the thirteen-field association, the Run material, generation-0 retained availability and no pins with nothing visible to another connection until its one COMMIT, after which the pair joins the admitted attempt with settlement pending; the receipt counter orders stored canonical decimals by length then bytes (2, 9, 10, 100 give 101) and refuses a full u64 on the invariant row; a SEAL binding whose RunId, carrier digest or operationRef does not join stages nothing; an error from the evidence COMMIT is undetermined with the attempt still admitted; the publication reserve equals exactly what attempt admission and the objects charge, and one byte short refuses on the budget row before the attempt row and any object; a reused ExecutionId is refused before any object; every ledger row maps to its existing termination; and x3d.publish.published is placed once, after the one PublishedCommit construction.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/715/description"}}, {"after": "Storage's crash-matrix support surface (law X9 r1 item 6, unit X9-1), doc(hidden). Compiled only under the test-only crash-matrix feature, which no manifest enables from a dependency table and which the crate refuses in any build without debug assertions (law X9 r1 item 2), so it is absent from every release build. It forwards security's surface unchanged, law X9 r4 item 6's three driver entries included; the shared fixture gates live in security, so storage adds no second site. Its one item of its own is the child module run_candidate, the synthetic run candidate, which needs the evaluator (law X3d r8 item 13, unit X3d-3; law X9 r7 item 6), re-exported with its label, its replay limits and the distinct variant (law X9 r12, unit X9-3); it reaches security only through CommitSession's public getters and the shared test-support accessor, and returns inputs only, never a ReplayedRun. Apart from the forwarded driver entries, nothing here returns an authority type.", "before": "Storage's crash-matrix support surface (law X9 r1 item 6, unit X9-1), doc(hidden). Compiled only under the test-only crash-matrix feature, which no manifest enables from a dependency table and which the crate refuses in any build without debug assertions (law X9 r1 item 2), so it is absent from every release build. It forwards security's surface unchanged; the shared fixture gates live in security, so storage adds no second site. Nothing here returns an authority type.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/716/description"}}, {"after": "The synthetic run candidate (law X3d r8 item 13, unit X3d-3; law X9 r7 item 6), a child of storage's crash-matrix support surface, doc(hidden), and included as the same source file by storage's unit tests (commit_tests.rs) and, on macOS, by host's admission_tests.rs for unit X8c's behavioural refusal cases and by host's commit_matrix_tests.rs (under crash-matrix) for unit X9-5's F01 substituted variants. As part of the support surface it is compiled only under the test-only crash-matrix feature, which no manifest enables from a dependency table and which the crate refuses in any build without debug assertions (law X9 r1 item 2), so it is absent from every release build. Inputs only: from a live CommitSession it starts from the pinned corpus Run security's SEAL tests replay (journal-seal-cases.json, packet-0-original), rewrites the snapshot's projectId to CommitSession::project_id and the evaluator closure to CommitSession::core_evaluator_closure (contract successor EC1), never core_closure, retaining that closure's descriptor with its manifest blob (the TR-CORE inventory body) and its tree blobs from security's shared test-support accessor, recomputes every dependent input identity and blob digest by a reference rewrite to a fixpoint (arrays kept in canonical order), re-derives the outputs with the evaluator's public derive_evaluation, and builds the semantic evidence, seal and Run as replay_run checks them. It returns retained objects, blobs and the claimed RunId with the synthetic label, never a ReplayedRun: replay_run stays the only mint. synthetic_run_candidate_distinct (law X9 r12, unit X9-3) builds the same candidate for the same session, except that the snapshot's source file extensionless gets same-length salted bytes before the fixpoint rewrite, so every dependent id and digest, the re-derived outputs and the RunId differ, for a next writer whose project already committed the candidate's Run (rows F13, F14 and F15). Test-only helpers (cfg(test)) rebind only the project, and rename the evaluator closure to a given descriptor, for the mismatch and core-closure tests. Synthetic; no compiler qualification.", "before": "The synthetic run candidate (law X3d r8 item 13, unit X3d-3; law X9 r7 item 6), a child of storage's crash-matrix support surface, doc(hidden), and included by storage's unit tests (commit_tests.rs) as the same source file. As part of the support surface it is compiled only under the test-only crash-matrix feature, which no manifest enables from a dependency table and which the crate refuses in any build without debug assertions (law X9 r1 item 2), so it is absent from every release build. Inputs only: from a live CommitSession it starts from the pinned corpus Run security's SEAL tests replay (journal-seal-cases.json, packet-0-original), rewrites the snapshot's projectId to CommitSession::project_id and the evaluator closure to CommitSession::core_evaluator_closure (contract successor EC1), never core_closure, retaining that closure's descriptor with its manifest blob (the TR-CORE inventory body) and its tree blobs from security's shared test-support accessor, recomputes every dependent input identity and blob digest by a reference rewrite to a fixpoint (arrays kept in canonical order), re-derives the outputs with the evaluator's public derive_evaluation, and builds the semantic evidence, seal and Run as replay_run checks them. It returns retained objects, blobs and the claimed RunId with the synthetic label, never a ReplayedRun: replay_run stays the only mint. Test-only helpers (cfg(test)) rebind only the project, and rename the evaluator closure to a given descriptor, for the mismatch and core-closure tests. Synthetic; no compiler qualification.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/717/description"}}, {"after": "Publish one commit's objects and prepare, stage and commit its evidence-ledger transaction (law X3c r7 items 4 to 7 and 9 to 11; unit X3c-2), as project_ledger.rs's child module commit. Objects: publication takes the durably admitted attempt; every declared object's length and SHA-256 are checked, and every byte reserved on the operation ledger, before the first write, so a commit that cannot be reserved refuses on the budget row and is never truncated; each object is published into objects/sha256 through blob_store (private temporary file, file barrier, exclusive link, directory barrier) or, only after an exclusive-link collision with unchanged visibility, confirmed byte for byte with its own barriers; an unequal, short or long file, a second link, a shared-writable mode or a non-regular entry at the name is LEDGER.CORRUPT and never overwritten; a failure stops publication and nothing is deleted, renamed or reused. PreparedLedger: BEGIN IMMEDIATE with busy_timeout 0 on the admitted, whole-schema-verified ledger, taken only with the published set (so after every barrier); busy is LEDGER.BUSY_TIMEOUT and holds nothing; owned, single use, not Clone, no SQL surface, and Drop only rolls back; its next_commit_sequence allocates the next receipt counter of (store, N) in that open transaction through the ledger's one counter accessor, charged as one indexed read, before the receipt that carries it is built (unit X3d-2). Staging in the open transaction, charged with the COMMIT before the first insert: the exact receipt and association through stage_recovery_pair, the Run material, whose inventory's blob digests together with its typed objects' H digests must equal the published objects exactly, a blob equal to a frame counting once (unit X3d-2), the initial availability record, and the Run's pins as a first publication under the attempt's operationRef; any failure drops the transaction, so all rows or none. The owned PreparedLedgerCommit adapter's one consuming method performs only COMMIT: success is Committed, an error or lost connection is Undetermined (DURABILITY.COMMIT_FAILED with the ExecutionId retained), never retried or read back, and the attempt row is never settled. X3d holds the journal transaction, level 4 and the AdmissionPermit around these calls. X3c-2's object crash points and COMMIT fault hook exist only under cfg(test); law X9's barrier points here (an x3c.object scope around each object's publication, and x3c.evidence's begin, one point after each of the four stagings, and a fallible COMMIT whose injected fail-before or fail-after is the undetermined outcome) have a body only under the test-only crash-matrix feature (law X9 r1 item 5, unit X9-1). attempt_and_objects_cost is exactly what attempt admission (the verified open and the attempt transaction) and the objects' publication charge, for the facade's one publication reserve (law X3d r6 item 3 step 2, unit X3d-2), and h_digest gives a typed object identity's H digest, the raw SHA-256 of its H preimage frame, which the facade's plan and recovery's object reads also use. The storage facade (commit.rs, unit X3d-2) composes these calls, which project_ledger.rs re-exports to it, on the production location ProjectStoreLocation::selected.", "before": "Publish one commit's objects and prepare, stage and commit its evidence-ledger transaction (law X3c r7 items 4 to 7 and 9 to 11; unit X3c-2), as project_ledger.rs's child module commit. Objects: publication takes the durably admitted attempt; every declared object's length and SHA-256 are checked, and every byte reserved on the operation ledger, before the first write, so a commit that cannot be reserved refuses on the budget row and is never truncated; each object is published into objects/sha256 through blob_store (private temporary file, file barrier, exclusive link, directory barrier) or, only after an exclusive-link collision with unchanged visibility, confirmed byte for byte with its own barriers; an unequal, short or long file, a second link, a shared-writable mode or a non-regular entry at the name is LEDGER.CORRUPT and never overwritten; a failure stops publication and nothing is deleted, renamed or reused. PreparedLedger: BEGIN IMMEDIATE with busy_timeout 0 on the admitted, whole-schema-verified ledger, taken only with the published set (so after every barrier); busy is LEDGER.BUSY_TIMEOUT and holds nothing; owned, single use, not Clone, no SQL surface, and Drop only rolls back. Staging in the open transaction, charged with the COMMIT before the first insert: the exact receipt and association through stage_recovery_pair, the Run material whose blob digests must equal the published objects exactly, the initial availability record, and the Run's pins as a first publication under the attempt's operationRef; any failure drops the transaction, so all rows or none. The owned PreparedLedgerCommit adapter's one consuming method performs only COMMIT: success is Committed, an error or lost connection is Undetermined (DURABILITY.COMMIT_FAILED with the ExecutionId retained), never retried or read back, and the attempt row is never settled. X3d holds the journal transaction, level 4 and the AdmissionPermit around these calls. Crash points and a COMMIT fault hook exist only under cfg(test). Only tests construct a location.", "parent": {"bytes": 552176, "path": "docs/implementation/m2/repository-file-inventory.v134.json", "sha256": "626cd71996d79de5c0efd914438dd65b3123e701e774ccdad1f8f9681466c58a"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/files/723/description"}}, {"after": "Check X3c-2 on X3c-1's scratch location with a held test writer lease: objects published new (0600, one link, both barriers, no residue) then confirmed byte for byte by a second attempt without rewriting; a wrong length or digest or a repeated digest refused as the invariant row before any write; unequal, short and long bytes, a directory, a link, a shared-writable file and a second hard link at an object name refused as LEDGER.CORRUPT and left unchanged, with earlier objects kept; a commit short of budget refused before the first object; a crash at each object step (temporary write, before the file barrier, after the link, and before the directory barrier with the link lost) keeping earlier objects and the residue, the attempt row admitted and nothing staged, with the next attempt completing; a busy ledger refused at once holding nothing, and a held PreparedLedger busy to other writers; another attempt's objects refused; a staged commit invisible until COMMIT, then every row present and joined as recovery reads i