orrections/public-detail-registry.v1.json plus isolated evaluator3 members. Every owner joins the same closed registry; unknown names refuse. These details do not create D9 codes. Isolated additions: BASELINE.ENTRY_PROJECTION_CONFLICT, COMPARISON.CORRESPONDENCE_INCOMPLETE, EVALUATION.FINDING_JOIN_REFUSED, EVALUATION.MIXED_OUTPUT_MAJOR, EVALUATION.OUTPUT_BOUND_EXCEEDED, EVALUATION.PROOF_VERDICT_INCONSISTENT, EVALUATION.PROJECTION_INPUT_INCOMPLETE, EVALUATION.WORK_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED, QUERY.CURSOR_MISMATCH, QUERY.ENDPOINT_AMBIGUOUS, QUERY.ENDPOINT_UNKNOWN, QUERY.FACT_VIEW_UNAVAILABLE, QUERY.PARAMS_MALFORMED, QUERY.RELATION_UNSUPPORTED, QUERY.SCHEMA_MAJOR_UNSUPPORTED, QUERY.VIEW_AMBIGUOUS, QUERY.VIEW_UNKNOWN, REPAIR.TARGET_CORRESPONDENCE_UNAVAILABLE, REPAIR.TARGET_METADATA_AMBIGUOUS. Shared registry members this surface must preserve (root registers in both common enums): EVALUATION.INPUT_REFUSED (structural evaluator input failure with the exact diagnostic retained separately), EVALUATION.SELECTION_LIMIT (well-formed prospective request above the published bound), EVALUATION.REQUIRED_OUTPUT_OMITTED (missing required provider or host output pointer on the public surface, retaining its exact reference). Do not fork a second registration. CONFIG.INVALID is a D9ErrorCode and a DomainDetailCode; it is not an arbitrary DomainDetail for evaluator3 join/projection refusals. Root integrates. Output bound error is existing D9ErrorCode OUTPUT.SERIALIZATION_FAILED with faultCause output-serialization, never HOST.IO_FAILURE. C2PM-1 additionally selects native.closure-protocol-invalid under its exact successor public-detail registry. Existing isolated additions and all D9 meanings stay unchanged.", "parent": {"bytes": 64840, "path": "docs/implementation/m3/snapshot-plan-c/c2pm-1-r2/completion/product/common-v3.schema.json", "sha256": "7c53a967a2d2c039963bf8cfff7f403d618c67595125cd1a647b0e1fc755c060"}, "selector": {"jsonPointer": "/$defs/DomainDetailCode/description"}}, {"after": "Gene